924
00:03:41,010 --> 00:03:46,040
Mask of Falsehood

925
00:03:41,510 --> 00:03:43,440
It's here, it's here...

926
00:03:43,440 --> 00:03:45,210
It's finally here!

927
00:03:45,210 --> 00:03:47,340
All eyes will be right on me!

928
00:03:47,340 --> 00:03:50,750
Now that we've donned the latest in fashion 
from Comme Ãa du Mitsugoshi,

929
00:03:50,750 --> 00:03:53,720
the eyes of every girl 
on the street will be...

930
00:03:53,720 --> 00:03:55,520
laser-focused on us!

931
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:58,540
First they'll make a move, 
then comes the smooch!

932
00:03:58,540 --> 00:04:00,010
Guaranteed!

933
00:04:01,600 --> 00:04:03,700
<i>Comme Ãa du Mitsugoshi...</i>

934
00:04:03,700 --> 00:04:06,810
<i>Anything related to design 
probably came from Eta.</i>

935
00:04:07,110 --> 00:04:09,750
<i>First Gamma, then Beta and Epsilon...</i>

936
00:04:09,750 --> 00:04:13,100
<i>Man, every single one of them 
is just running wild.</i>

937
00:04:14,510 --> 00:04:16,170
Uh, something's peeling off.

938
00:04:16,170 --> 00:04:17,160
What?

939
00:04:17,160 --> 00:04:19,850
No! The Comme Ãa du Mitsogoshi logo!

940
00:04:19,850 --> 00:04:22,240
Without that, these clothes 
are just cheap knockoffs!

941
00:04:22,240 --> 00:04:23,800
But on the other hand,

942
00:04:23,800 --> 00:04:27,510
if we stick these to other clothes, they'll look like 
they come from Comme Ãa du Mitsugoshi...

943
00:04:29,610 --> 00:04:31,210
What a lame brand...

944
00:04:31,890 --> 00:04:34,330
This is the logo of 
the place we bought these from!

945
00:04:34,330 --> 00:04:36,130
Does this mean mine is, too?

946
00:04:36,130 --> 00:04:39,220
And now that I look at this up close,
 it seems kinda off.

947
00:04:39,220 --> 00:04:42,000
The real one is more, y'know, 
intricate or something.

948
00:04:42,710 --> 00:04:45,010
No wonder these duds were so cheap.

949
00:04:45,010 --> 00:04:45,840
Mine, too...

950
00:04:45,840 --> 00:04:49,400
<i>Come to think of it, all my outfits 
were curated by Alpha and the girls.</i><i></i>

951
00:04:50,010 --> 00:04:53,360
<i>Everything I'm wearing is like 
a knockoff from my past life.</i>

952
00:04:55,000 --> 00:05:00,420
<i>I saw people walking around the capital wearing suits 
and thought it was just the culture here.</i><i></i>

953
00:05:00,420 --> 00:05:03,000
<i>But it's looking like 
that was all Alpha's doing, too.</i>

954
00:05:03,830 --> 00:05:08,780
<i>Guess they're using my knowledge from my past life 
to increase their market share as far as they can make it go.</i><i></i>

955
00:05:08,780 --> 00:05:13,510
<i>And I bet the people they're stealing business from 
are none too happy about it.</i>

956
00:05:13,810 --> 00:05:17,640
<i>The people they're stealing business from!</i>

957
00:05:17,640 --> 00:05:19,300
<i>They aren't happy!</i><i></i>

958
00:05:20,160 --> 00:05:21,930
But that all ends today.

959
00:05:22,810 --> 00:05:23,840
Cid?

960
00:05:23,840 --> 00:05:25,170
Taking a dump?

961
00:05:25,170 --> 00:05:26,380
No.

962
00:05:27,210 --> 00:05:29,380
I'm gonna reclaim what's mine.

963
00:05:29,380 --> 00:05:30,230
All of it.

964
00:05:30,590 --> 00:05:31,840
What's that about?

965
00:05:31,840 --> 00:05:35,190
Doesn't he know that summer's already over?

966
00:05:45,190 --> 00:05:46,730
As of today...

967
00:05:47,400 --> 00:05:49,400
I am a super elite secret agent!

968
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:52,650
And tonight, the world...

969
00:05:53,150 --> 00:05:54,380
shall know my name!

970
00:06:01,110 --> 00:06:02,500
Welcome...

971
00:06:04,900 --> 00:06:06,510
my dear Shadow.

972
00:06:07,810 --> 00:06:09,310
I have forsaken that name.

973
00:06:09,610 --> 00:06:11,540
Oh yes, of course,

974
00:06:11,540 --> 00:06:13,460
Mr. John Smith.

975
00:06:13,460 --> 00:06:17,400
It is truly heartening to have you 
so kindly joining our ranks.

976
00:06:17,760 --> 00:06:21,210
It is a profitable arrangement 
for me, that is all.

977
00:06:21,210 --> 00:06:25,290
Oh, but don't you find it depressing to maintain 
a relationship based solely on profit?

978
00:06:25,290 --> 00:06:26,370
Don't you?

979
00:06:26,600 --> 00:06:28,300
My, how unfriendly.

980
00:06:29,910 --> 00:06:35,040
The other day, Garter called a meeting 
of the Major Corporate Alliance.

981
00:06:35,340 --> 00:06:38,750
Something about strengthening 
their measures against Mitsugoshi.

982
00:06:39,320 --> 00:06:44,130
The fall of Mitsugoshi may come sooner 
than we had anticipated.

983
00:06:44,130 --> 00:06:45,220
I see.

984
00:06:45,500 --> 00:06:48,540
Our plan remains unchanged.

985
00:06:48,540 --> 00:06:52,940
While Mitsugoshi and the Major Corporate Alliance 
work to destroy each other...

986
00:06:52,940 --> 00:06:54,900
We take everything.

987
00:06:55,420 --> 00:06:58,750
We will need you to take action 
for us, Mr. Smith.

988
00:06:58,750 --> 00:07:00,920
But do be careful.

989
00:07:00,920 --> 00:07:04,860
Behind the Major Corporate Alliance, 
you will find <i>him</i>.

990
00:07:05,380 --> 00:07:07,790
The underworld swordsman 
who rose above Garter

991
00:07:07,790 --> 00:07:12,110
and took control of the MCA 
before anyone knew what was happening.

992
00:07:12,110 --> 00:07:14,040
Gettan the Sword Devil.

993
00:07:14,040 --> 00:07:16,540
I know the man well.

994
00:07:17,110 --> 00:07:21,250
He's a dangerous cur who will stop 
at nothing to get what he wants.

995
00:07:22,310 --> 00:07:24,020
Leave him to me.

996
00:07:24,020 --> 00:07:25,900
I swear I'll...

997
00:07:36,350 --> 00:07:38,400
I look forward to seeing it.

998
00:07:39,510 --> 00:07:43,110
In the battle for control 
over the market in the Royal Capital...

999
00:07:43,110 --> 00:07:45,790
At the end of the conflict 
where money is bought with blood,

1000
00:07:45,790 --> 00:07:48,730
who will remain standing in the end?

1001
00:07:48,730 --> 00:07:51,830
I will destroy it all, 
then build it up again.

1002
00:07:55,010 --> 00:07:56,500
The moment you've all been waiting for!

1003
00:07:56,500 --> 00:07:59,580
The Garter Corporation, 
friend to every family's budget,

1004
00:07:59,580 --> 00:08:02,800
starts our big autumn sale right now!

1005
00:08:03,300 --> 00:08:04,420
Listen up.

1006
00:08:04,420 --> 00:08:06,790
The battle we're about to face is 
where blood is wiped away with more bloodâ

1007
00:08:06,790 --> 00:08:08,000
Outta my way!

1008
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:09,000
Our target is 50% offâ

1009
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:10,150
Move it!

1010
00:08:11,600 --> 00:08:13,600
Step right up and have a look over here!

1011
00:08:13,600 --> 00:08:16,940
Garter's not the only one! Today we have 
bargain prices on everything in stock!

1012
00:08:16,940 --> 00:08:20,150
Check out the selection 
at local hidden gem, Highway Robert's!

1013
00:08:21,040 --> 00:08:23,600
<i>Major sales all across 
the shopping district.</i>

1014
00:08:23,600 --> 00:08:26,460
We won't let Mitsugoshi get us down!

1015
00:08:26,460 --> 00:08:30,230
<i>So basically, 
Alpha and the girls have gone too far.</i>

1016
00:08:30,230 --> 00:08:33,920
<i>They're selling exclusive products 
with no concern for local distributors.</i><i></i>

1017
00:08:33,920 --> 00:08:39,020
<i>And now, they've made enemies of the big corporations, 
and even the downtown shopping district has it in for them.</i>

1018
00:08:39,510 --> 00:08:42,290
<i>Now that they've earned 
the loathing of the entire industry...</i><i></i>

1019
00:08:42,290 --> 00:08:43,840
<i>Yeah, Yukime was right.</i>

1020
00:08:43,840 --> 00:08:46,760
<i>The future of Mitsugoshi 
is pretty much devoid of all hope.</i>

1021
00:08:47,300 --> 00:08:49,730
I will destroy it all, 
then build it up again.

1022
00:08:50,610 --> 00:08:54,500
<i>They will crush Mitsugoshi for me, 
and I will crush them in turn.</i><i></i>

1023
00:08:54,500 --> 00:09:00,540
<i>I will use the massive amounts of capital that remain 
to move to a brand new market and start up a new corporation.</i>

1024
00:09:00,540 --> 00:09:03,340
<i>I'll invite Alpha and the girls 
as upper management.</i><i></i>

1025
00:09:03,340 --> 00:09:07,400
<i>Change the name, 
and Mitsugoshi will be reborn.</i><i></i>

1026
00:09:08,010 --> 00:09:11,310
<i>Once it's all over, then they'll understand.</i>

1027
00:09:11,960 --> 00:09:14,330
<i>They'll know this was the best choice.</i>

1028
00:09:16,040 --> 00:09:18,400
That's out of five thousand zeni?

1029
00:09:18,400 --> 00:09:20,800
"You break it, you buy it"?

1030
00:09:20,800 --> 00:09:23,840
This is why people like Mitsugoshi better.

1031
00:09:23,840 --> 00:09:25,320
What did you expect?

1032
00:09:25,320 --> 00:09:28,300
That's 1,750 zeni in change!

1033
00:09:29,290 --> 00:09:31,130
Is it me, or does that bill look wrong?

1034
00:09:31,130 --> 00:09:32,900
Wrong how?

1035
00:09:32,900 --> 00:09:34,850
I don't remember that being the design.

1036
00:09:34,850 --> 00:09:36,770
Oh, it's one of those, y'know.

1037
00:09:37,110 --> 00:09:40,410
The new bills put out 
by the Major Corporate Alliance.

1038
00:09:40,410 --> 00:09:44,100
That's why everything's on sale today, remember? 
To commemorate the release of the new bill.

1039
00:09:44,420 --> 00:09:47,000
So, what were we using before this one?

1040
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:48,060
Here.

1041
00:09:48,390 --> 00:09:50,310
From the Mitsugoshi Bank.

1042
00:09:50,310 --> 00:09:51,700
Mitsugoshi...

1043
00:09:52,020 --> 00:09:55,590
Before, only official Mitsugoshi storefronts 
would accept them.

1044
00:09:55,590 --> 00:09:58,240
But now, we can use them all over the city.

1045
00:09:58,240 --> 00:10:01,500
<i>Those punks have their own bank now, too?</i>

1046
00:09:58,710 --> 00:10:02,210
I tried to use one with a traveling merchant 
over summer break...

1047
00:10:03,410 --> 00:10:04,960
<i>Now that I think of it,</i>

1048
00:10:04,960 --> 00:10:11,970
<i>I do remember babbling some random facts I saw 
on an MHK documentary about banks and credit creation...</i>

1049
00:10:11,970 --> 00:10:14,790
But even if there is polarity 
in the market...

1050
00:10:14,790 --> 00:10:18,090
In that case, find a different provider 
for a different price.

1051
00:10:18,090 --> 00:10:20,540
<i>But my memories of it were so fuzzy,</i>

1052
00:10:18,090 --> 00:10:20,540
But liquidity isn't a constant.

1053
00:10:20,540 --> 00:10:22,400
<i>and I ended that conversation fast.</i>

1054
00:10:20,540 --> 00:10:22,400
It rises and falls dramatically.

1055
00:10:22,890 --> 00:10:26,670
<i>But those girls took that 
MHK information and ran with it.</i>

1056
00:10:26,670 --> 00:10:30,790
<i>Not only did they establish their own bank, 
they managed to issue their own paper currency!</i><i></i>

1057
00:10:31,310 --> 00:10:33,000
<i>And they've even inspired copies...</i>

1058
00:10:31,310 --> 00:10:33,000
What do we do next?

1059
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:34,940
<i>I mean, respectful homages.</i>

1060
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:34,940
How about karaoke or something?

1061
00:10:34,940 --> 00:10:36,290
<i>Copies?</i>

1062
00:10:37,010 --> 00:10:41,710
<i>The Mitsugoshi banknote uses multicolor printing 
and a carefully placed watermark.</i>

1063
00:10:41,710 --> 00:10:45,500
<i>But this copycat version 
has cruder printing and a simpler design...</i>

1064
00:10:46,130 --> 00:10:47,290
<i>That means...</i>

1065
00:10:48,900 --> 00:10:51,350
When I was a child, I had a dream.

1066
00:10:53,200 --> 00:10:56,670
I had a thousand yen bill left 
from my New Year's allowance, and I thought...

1067
00:10:56,670 --> 00:11:00,590
Maybe I could make more of them 
with the copy machine at the corner store.

1068
00:11:00,590 --> 00:11:01,790
The <i>what</i> now?

1069
00:11:01,790 --> 00:11:03,980
Who cares? Gimme my money back.

1070
00:11:04,720 --> 00:11:09,690
I gave up on the idea after the old man 
at the counter yelled his head off.

1071
00:11:09,690 --> 00:11:10,670
What is this about?

1072
00:11:10,670 --> 00:11:12,300
Cid, my money.

1073
00:11:12,690 --> 00:11:14,810
But now...

1074
00:11:14,810 --> 00:11:16,900
I'm a super elite secret agent.

1075
00:11:17,290 --> 00:11:19,120
And dreams can come true!

1076
00:11:19,120 --> 00:11:20,130
Cid!

1077
00:11:20,130 --> 00:11:20,740
Hey, Cid!

1078
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:22,950
Come on, brain! Remember!

1079
00:11:23,370 --> 00:11:25,380
I'm counting on you, MHK!

1080
00:11:25,380 --> 00:11:26,630
Cid!

1081
00:11:26,630 --> 00:11:28,900
Cid, my money!

1082
00:11:29,960 --> 00:11:29,960


1083
00:11:34,410 --> 00:11:37,800
This single gold coin multiplies 
into several times what it was.

1084
00:11:38,210 --> 00:11:42,650
But what we find there is 
the fleeting illusion we call "credit".

1085
00:11:45,710 --> 00:11:48,810
Are you, perchance, 
talking about paper money?

1086
00:11:49,080 --> 00:11:52,340
These scraps of paper, considered by the masses 
to be no different than currency,

1087
00:11:52,340 --> 00:11:54,040
are, more precisely, not currency at all.

1088
00:11:54,040 --> 00:11:57,730
In reality, they're no more than claim checks 
for coins that have been left in the care of the bank.

1089
00:11:58,280 --> 00:12:01,410
Let's say, for example, 
you've put ten thousand zeni in the bank.

1090
00:12:01,410 --> 00:12:06,790
In exchange, you're given a banknote for ten thousand zeni, 
which you can use to purchase goods and services.

1091
00:12:06,790 --> 00:12:10,170
But this is where something strange occurs.

1092
00:12:10,900 --> 00:12:14,150
You have ten thousand zeni in the bank 
and ten thousand zeni in a banknote.

1093
00:12:14,590 --> 00:12:17,700
At some point, your zeni 
has doubled to twenty thousand.

1094
00:12:18,500 --> 00:12:23,290
If the ten thousand zeni in the bank remains 
dormant in its vault, there is no problem.

1095
00:12:23,290 --> 00:12:26,400
Because, even if the money had, 
in fact, doubled,

1096
00:12:26,400 --> 00:12:31,060
as long as only the original ten thousand zeni circulates through 
the market, there is no contradiction.

1097
00:12:31,670 --> 00:12:34,710
But the bank has used 
the ten thousand zeni deposited there

1098
00:12:34,710 --> 00:12:36,650
as collateral to lend out even more money.

1099
00:12:37,070 --> 00:12:41,840
The prosperous economy of the capital stemmed 
from the business developments of Mitsugoshi itself.

1100
00:12:41,840 --> 00:12:45,650
Seeing a good opportunity, 
the merchants wished to borrow some capital,

1101
00:12:45,650 --> 00:12:49,500
and the bank met the demand 
by supplying paper money.

1102
00:12:49,710 --> 00:12:52,850
No one wants to walk around 
with heavy coins in their wallets.

1103
00:12:52,850 --> 00:12:57,460
Use of paper money spread like wildfire, 
further obscuring the currency's true value.

1104
00:12:57,710 --> 00:13:02,200
The ten thousand zeni in the vault, multiplied to several times 
what it was, circulated throughout the capital.

1105
00:13:02,200 --> 00:13:06,200
And Mitsugoshi gained exponential profits 
by reaping the rewards of the interest.

1106
00:13:06,790 --> 00:13:09,440
This is the true value of credit creation.

1107
00:13:09,440 --> 00:13:11,610
"Credit creation"...

1108
00:13:11,610 --> 00:13:13,710
What a fitting expression.

1109
00:13:13,710 --> 00:13:19,850
Through these means, a scrap of paper not even worth 
a copper coin is given more value than gold.

1110
00:13:19,850 --> 00:13:23,150
The leader of the Mitsugoshi Bank must be 
an extraordinary con artist.

1111
00:13:23,710 --> 00:13:25,810
What might this person be like, I wonder?

1112
00:13:25,810 --> 00:13:28,700
If I ever have the chance, I would love 
to have a chat with this individual.

1113
00:13:29,720 --> 00:13:34,590
But is a piece of paper truly worth 
the credit people give it?

1114
00:13:37,790 --> 00:13:39,810
Do you notice anything 
different between the two?

1115
00:13:40,790 --> 00:13:43,590
You mean the presence 
of a watermark in one but not the other?

1116
00:13:43,590 --> 00:13:47,270
And, I might add, the Major Corporate Alliance bill 
has a rougher design.

1117
00:13:47,590 --> 00:13:50,200
Rougher printing, rougher edges...

1118
00:13:50,200 --> 00:13:52,230
Do you know what this means?

1119
00:13:54,300 --> 00:13:56,190
It would be easy to fake?

1120
00:13:58,170 --> 00:14:00,000
We create fake money.

1121
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:02,500
And we'll make a fortune 
in counterfeit bills!

1122
00:14:06,500 --> 00:14:08,290
Excuse me, Mr. Smith.

1123
00:14:09,010 --> 00:14:11,290
As you are no doubt aware,

1124
00:14:11,290 --> 00:14:15,300
the Major Corporate Alliance bills 
are still only in circulation in the Royal Capital.

1125
00:14:15,800 --> 00:14:19,250
If we forged them, the authorities would 
immediately trace them to the source.

1126
00:14:19,570 --> 00:14:20,210
Huh?!

1127
00:14:20,810 --> 00:14:24,300
If done on a small scale, 
I'm sure it could be accomplished without discovery.

1128
00:14:24,300 --> 00:14:26,810
But the amount we'd earn would be 
hardly more than a child's allowance.

1129
00:14:27,210 --> 00:14:29,210
How do you propose weâ

1130
00:14:33,480 --> 00:14:34,880
Mr.â

1131
00:14:34,880 --> 00:14:36,440
Is that really...

1132
00:14:36,900 --> 00:14:38,900
Is that really what you think?

1133
00:14:41,130 --> 00:14:43,640
This is the true value of credit creation.

1134
00:14:45,250 --> 00:14:46,690
You can't mean...

1135
00:14:47,200 --> 00:14:51,540
If we did make and circulate a large quantity 
of counterfeit bills in a short period of time,

1136
00:14:51,540 --> 00:14:53,250
naturally we would be discovered.

1137
00:14:53,250 --> 00:14:57,670
And rumors of the bills would reach the ears 
of the general public almost immediately.

1138
00:14:57,920 --> 00:15:02,380
At that point, the citizens would harbor doubts 
about the contents of their own wallets.

1139
00:15:02,710 --> 00:15:05,610
The credit given 
to that paper would be lost!

1140
00:15:05,610 --> 00:15:06,350
Huh?!

1141
00:15:06,620 --> 00:15:09,290
The discovery of the counterfeiting 
was already integrated into the plan...

1142
00:15:09,290 --> 00:15:11,720
No, the discovery <i>was</i> the plan!

1143
00:15:11,720 --> 00:15:14,010
When the people start to doubt 
the value of the paper,

1144
00:15:14,010 --> 00:15:16,910
they'll make a run to the bank 
and exchange it for gold!

1145
00:15:16,910 --> 00:15:20,910
If we're one step ahead of the game, 
we can monopolize the profits!

1146
00:15:20,910 --> 00:15:22,600
That's what you've been planning all along!

1147
00:15:28,570 --> 00:15:29,900
Is that really...

1148
00:15:30,530 --> 00:15:32,270
what you think?

1149
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:42,090
Yes.

1150
00:15:42,380 --> 00:15:43,900
It is what I think.

1151
00:15:45,410 --> 00:15:49,510
This plan... is utterly flawless.

1152
00:15:59,700 --> 00:16:01,900
That is exactly right.

1153
00:16:10,020 --> 00:16:12,700
In the end, he was testing my sincerity.

1154
00:16:13,340 --> 00:16:17,060
If I had given in to the pressure 
and rattled off some thoughtless babblings,

1155
00:16:17,060 --> 00:16:18,150
then I...

1156
00:16:19,960 --> 00:16:21,980
John Smith...

1157
00:16:21,980 --> 00:16:24,810
The man formerly known as Shadow...

1158
00:16:38,840 --> 00:16:43,010
<i>The mysterious man secretly scheming while Mitsugoshi 
and the Major Corporate Alliance battle it out,</i>

1159
00:16:43,010 --> 00:16:44,440
<i>John Smith.</i>

1160
00:16:44,440 --> 00:16:47,960
<i>He hides his identity 
and carries out his mission alone.</i>

1161
00:16:47,960 --> 00:16:52,900
<i>I am the man who betrays his organization in order 
to save it, the Super Elite Secret Agent.</i>

1162
00:16:53,280 --> 00:16:55,500
<i>What could be cooler than that?</i>

1163
00:16:55,960 --> 00:16:57,500
Gimme more, Boss!

1164
00:17:00,420 --> 00:17:02,490
<i>What does she think she's doing?</i>

1165
00:17:02,490 --> 00:17:03,880
Gimme more, Boss!

1166
00:17:03,880 --> 00:17:05,400
Gimme more!

1167
00:17:14,210 --> 00:17:15,800
You smell like foxes.

1168
00:17:15,800 --> 00:17:17,540
Yeah, I was hanging out withâ

1169
00:17:17,540 --> 00:17:19,200
I was out hunting foxes.

1170
00:17:19,200 --> 00:17:20,190
Hunting?!

1171
00:17:20,190 --> 00:17:21,660
Delta wants to hunt!

1172
00:17:21,660 --> 00:17:24,300
Sorry, the fox is already hunted.

1173
00:17:24,300 --> 00:17:26,250
And would you get off me already?

1174
00:17:26,250 --> 00:17:26,810
No!

1175
00:17:26,810 --> 00:17:29,000
What are you doing in the capital anyâ

1176
00:17:30,310 --> 00:17:34,120
Delta woke up early this morning, 
ate lots and lots of meat,

1177
00:17:34,120 --> 00:17:35,900
and came to the capital 
for the first time in forever!

1178
00:17:35,900 --> 00:17:37,520
So, why did you come to the capital?

1179
00:17:37,770 --> 00:17:39,500
Delta was hunting!

1180
00:17:39,500 --> 00:17:41,200
And why were you hunting?

1181
00:17:41,200 --> 00:17:43,060
Delta did so much hunting!

1182
00:17:43,060 --> 00:17:44,460
Wanna hunt with me, Boss?

1183
00:17:44,460 --> 00:17:46,040
Why were you hunting?

1184
00:17:46,040 --> 00:17:47,810
Lady Alpha told me to!

1185
00:17:47,810 --> 00:17:49,210
Wanna hunt with me, Boss?

1186
00:17:49,710 --> 00:17:51,210
So, it was Alpha's orders?

1187
00:17:51,210 --> 00:17:52,150
Uh-huh!

1188
00:17:52,150 --> 00:17:53,600
Wanna hunt with me, Boss?

1189
00:17:53,600 --> 00:17:55,210
What have you been hunting?

1190
00:17:55,210 --> 00:17:58,000
Bandits! You like hunting bandits too, Boss!

1191
00:17:58,000 --> 00:18:01,190
Yeah, I do like hunting bandits.

1192
00:18:01,190 --> 00:18:02,570
Hunt with me!

1193
00:18:02,570 --> 00:18:04,290
I don't think I can right now.

1194
00:18:04,290 --> 00:18:05,700
No, hunt with me!

1195
00:18:05,700 --> 00:18:07,100
Hold your horses.

1196
00:18:07,100 --> 00:18:09,900
Didn't you come to the capital 
for a specific reason?

1197
00:18:10,310 --> 00:18:11,690
Reason?

1198
00:18:11,690 --> 00:18:13,610
Didn't Alpha wanna see you?

1199
00:18:14,910 --> 00:18:15,870
Lady Alpha!

1200
00:18:16,120 --> 00:18:17,170
Did you forget?

1201
00:18:17,170 --> 00:18:18,450
Yeah, I forgot.

1202
00:18:18,900 --> 00:18:20,370
She's gonna be so mad at me!

1203
00:18:20,880 --> 00:18:22,420
You'd better hurry and see her.

1204
00:18:23,470 --> 00:18:25,610
But our bandit hunt...

1205
00:18:27,670 --> 00:18:33,310
<i>Looking at Delta reminds me of John, 
the pet I had in my past life.</i>

1206
00:18:33,730 --> 00:18:36,440
Body found dead of unknown cause. Fourth incident this month.

1207
00:18:33,730 --> 00:18:36,440
Body found dead of unknown cause. Fourth incident this month.

1208
00:18:34,500 --> 00:18:36,440
Another failure?

1209
00:18:36,440 --> 00:18:40,700
Yes, um, their private soldiers 
are more powerful than we anticipated.

1210
00:18:40,700 --> 00:18:43,790
So, the would-be bandits are useless.

1211
00:18:43,790 --> 00:18:45,900
In that case, 
I'll send the Clovers after them.

1212
00:18:45,900 --> 00:18:47,700
The Clovers?

1213
00:18:47,700 --> 00:18:50,900
The elite assassins you 
hand-picked yourself, Mr. Gettan?

1214
00:18:50,900 --> 00:18:54,850
With them on the job, 
Mitsugoshi's secrets are as good as ours!

1215
00:19:06,920 --> 00:19:09,670
<i>Delta is fundamentally incapable 
of following the command "stay".</i><i></i>

1216
00:19:09,670 --> 00:19:12,460
<i>Her brand of hunting 
is a one-sided massacre.</i>

1217
00:19:12,460 --> 00:19:14,940
<i>Makes gathering treasure that much easier...</i><i></i>

1218
00:19:15,420 --> 00:19:18,590
But I miss out on the element 
of enjoying the battle.

1219
00:19:18,590 --> 00:19:20,300
Stop! Wait a minute!

1220
00:19:21,210 --> 00:19:23,370
You're Sara, aren't you? It's me!

1221
00:19:23,370 --> 00:19:24,920
You know? Me! Me!

1222
00:19:24,920 --> 00:19:26,890
It's me, Zabra!

1223
00:19:26,890 --> 00:19:28,480
You remember, don't you, Sara?

1224
00:19:30,910 --> 00:19:32,700
You smell like my dad.

1225
00:19:32,700 --> 00:19:33,880
That's right!

1226
00:19:33,880 --> 00:19:36,410
I'm your older brother, Zabra.

1227
00:19:36,410 --> 00:19:38,810
But how are you even alive?

1228
00:19:38,810 --> 00:19:41,120
I heard you got possessed and hunted by Dad.

1229
00:19:41,810 --> 00:19:44,590
Delta is the best at hide-and-seek.

1230
00:19:44,590 --> 00:19:47,830
Delta? Is that what you call yourself now?

1231
00:19:48,100 --> 00:19:50,540
Anyway, Sara, you can just let me go, right?

1232
00:19:50,540 --> 00:19:52,900
I'm working for the great Gettan now.

1233
00:19:52,900 --> 00:19:54,810
You know him right? The legendaryâ

1234
00:19:55,960 --> 00:19:58,020
Don't want a weak sibling.

1235
00:19:58,020 --> 00:20:01,090
Sure that's okay?? He <i>was</i> your brother.

1236
00:20:01,670 --> 00:20:04,290
Weaklings bring shame to the family.

1237
00:20:04,290 --> 00:20:05,700
Oh, okay.

1238
00:20:05,700 --> 00:20:08,000
Delta's dad is the chief of our clan!

1239
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:11,480
He has lots of lovers, 
and over a thousand children!

1240
00:20:11,480 --> 00:20:14,150
Right. Then I guess one less won't hurt him.

1241
00:20:14,150 --> 00:20:15,870
The weak die.

1242
00:20:15,870 --> 00:20:18,880
If there aren't enough, we make more. 
That's the law of the clan!

1243
00:20:18,880 --> 00:20:21,370
<i>That's a therianthrope for you. 
They do things on a different scale.</i>

1244
00:20:21,610 --> 00:20:24,450
<i>You do find the occasional intelligent kind,</i><i></i>

1245
00:20:24,450 --> 00:20:28,420
<i>but there's a reason most people assume 
they're a bunch of "might makes right" types.</i>

1246
00:20:28,700 --> 00:20:32,060
Maybe I should go visit 
the therianthrope lands sometime.

1247
00:20:32,060 --> 00:20:34,380
Oh, I just had a great idea!

1248
00:20:34,710 --> 00:20:36,440
You can be our chief, Boss!

1249
00:20:36,440 --> 00:20:37,500
What?

1250
00:20:37,500 --> 00:20:39,350
If you beat my dad, you'll be the chief!

1251
00:20:39,600 --> 00:20:42,640
Then you can have lots of babies, 
and we'll be the strongest clan ever!

1252
00:20:42,640 --> 00:20:43,750
Not happening.

1253
00:20:43,750 --> 00:20:46,190
Yes, happening! 
I'll get a hundred women for you!

1254
00:20:46,480 --> 00:20:48,140
And Delta will have a hundred babies!

1255
00:20:48,140 --> 00:20:49,500
No way, not a chance.

1256
00:20:49,500 --> 00:20:51,810
This hunt is over. We're going home.

1257
00:20:54,840 --> 00:20:56,670
Zabra has been defeated, you say?

1258
00:20:56,670 --> 00:20:57,840
Yes, sir.

1259
00:20:57,840 --> 00:21:02,100
One of our underground hideouts was attacked, 
and we found his body inside.

1260
00:21:02,100 --> 00:21:04,900
And, um, Mr. Gettan...

1261
00:21:04,900 --> 00:21:09,000
In these last few months, 
our numbers have been reduced to practically nothing.

1262
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:13,080
If this keeps up, it'll affect the personnel 
we have running our public enterprises.

1263
00:21:13,310 --> 00:21:17,190
We invested a fair deal 
of capital in establishing our bank.

1264
00:21:17,190 --> 00:21:21,920
And the amount of money that went to bribing the legislators 
to let us print our money is nothing to be sneezed at.

1265
00:21:21,920 --> 00:21:25,060
What do you say to stepping back 
and reevaluatingâ

1266
00:21:25,060 --> 00:21:26,380
Garter...

1267
00:21:27,250 --> 00:21:30,310
Your purpose is to control all commerce in the city.

1268
00:21:30,880 --> 00:21:34,940
Surely you haven't forgotten who it was 
that put you in that position?

1269
00:21:34,940 --> 00:21:37,640
N-No, sir! Of course I haven't!

1270
00:21:37,640 --> 00:21:40,730
All you need to do is follow orders...

1271
00:21:40,730 --> 00:21:42,500
<i>My</i> orders.

1272
00:21:44,620 --> 00:21:48,040
At any rate, 
Zabra was the weakest of the Clovers.

1273
00:21:48,400 --> 00:21:50,600
Summon the three that are left.

1274
00:21:51,010 --> 00:21:54,980
Strengthen our offense against Mitsugoshi,
 and take all their trade secrets.

1275
00:21:54,980 --> 00:21:56,400
Y-Yes, sir!

1276
00:21:59,510 --> 00:22:02,930
Mitsugoshi is tougher than I thought.

1277
00:22:03,210 --> 00:22:06,440
Now I see why the Cult 
labeled them as a threat.

